From: alvesmaicon <alvesmaiconn@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: sun8i-codec-analog: keep HPCOM powered

DAPM powers HPCOM and its protection up with the headphone amplifier for
every stream and down after it. With the jack's return on HPCOM (direct
drive), powering it down with headphones in pops loudly and resets the
whole analog block to its defaults (headphone volume to 0, the PA muted,
every gain back to 0 dB).

The vendor driver sets HPCOM_FC and COMPTEN once at init and never
clears them. Do the same: force HPCOM and its protection on when the
headphone widgets are added. The amplifier keeps following the streams.

The amplifier stays out of this on purpose. With it on, plugging
headphones in or pulling them out clicks loudly, every time; with it off
and HPCOM on, the jack is silent. With HPCOM off as well, it clicks
again. Powering the amplifier up or down with headphones in and HPCOM on
only gives a faint hiss.

diff --git a/sound/soc/sunxi/sun8i-codec-analog.c b/sound/soc/sunxi/sun8i-codec-analog.c
--- a/sound/soc/sunxi/sun8i-codec-analog.c
+++ b/sound/soc/sunxi/sun8i-codec-analog.c
@@ -416,6 +416,16 @@ static int sun8i_codec_add_headphone(struct snd_soc_component *cmpnt)
 		return ret;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * With the jack's return on HPCOM, powering HPCOM up or down with
+	 * headphones in pops and resets the analog block to its defaults.
+	 * The vendor driver sets it up once: keep it and its protection on.
+	 * The amplifier still follows the streams: on, it clicks whenever a
+	 * plug goes in or out.
+	 */
+	snd_soc_dapm_force_enable_pin(dapm, "HPCOM");
+	snd_soc_dapm_force_enable_pin(dapm, "HPCOM Protection");
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
